 ### [Camera Setup and Projection Matrix Construction](3965-camera-setup-and-projection-matrix-construction.md)
 This method initializes camera parameters for volume rendering or training, handling downscaling, view matrix construction, and projection matrix calculation. It differs from generic graphics pipelines by explicitly managing intrinsic scaling for multi-resolution training and constructing a specific projection matrix tailored for the near/far plane constraints of the rendering engine.
+
+### Lazy Camera Matrix Update
+Computes view and projection matrices only when camera state changes, using dirty flags to avoid redundant matrix multiplications [S5, unofficial]. It tracks `view_dirty` and `projection_dirty` boolean flags, setting them on position/orientation or viewport resize changes respectively [S5, unofficial]. When requested, it checks flags, computes $V = R(\text{elevation}, \text{azimuth}) \cdot T(-\mathbf{p})$ if `view_dirty`, and $P = \text{perspective}(\text{fov}, \text{aspect\_ratio}, z_{\text{near}}, z_{\text{far}})$ if `projection_dirty`, then combines them [S5, unofficial]. It enforces a `max_elevation` of $85.0^\circ$ to prevent gimbal lock, and handles negative azimuth values from `fmodf` by adding $360.0^\circ$ [S5, unofficial].
 
